-- EXPECT-ERROR: cannot have a type annotation
-- A `let?` binding takes NO type annotation (the bound type is inferred from
-- the Result's Ok payload). The dedicated diagnostic — the `LET QUESTION
-- simple_pattern COLON error` production (parser.mly, 2026-07-13) — points at
-- the annotation, rather than the generic missing-`=` recovery it used to hit.
mod R15LetqTypeAnnotation do
  fn f() : Result(Int, String) do Ok(1) end
  fn bad() : Result(Int, String) do
    let? x : Int = f()
    Ok(x)
  end
end
